SquadReplay Agent Source-Available License 1.1

Copyright (c) 2026 BlueMoonTR / the SquadReplay project.

This repository contains the source code of the SquadReplay agent -- the
program that runs on a Squad dedicated game server, reads live match data
from the game process's memory, and sends it to a SquadReplay central server
(squadreplay.com). It is published as single-file variants so that anyone
considering running one on their own server can read exactly what it does
before trusting it: which files it reads and writes, which network endpoints
it contacts, and the process-memory access it needs.

This license applies to versions 0.86.0 and later. Versions published earlier
remain available under the terms (version 1.0) they were published with.

1. Definitions

"The Software" means the source code and documentation contained in this
repository, and any portion or modification of it.

"The Central Service" means the SquadReplay central server and everything it
provides to a running agent: the signed code modules ("payloads"), the
configuration it serves, and the network protocol used to talk to it. The
Central Service is NOT part of the Software and is not licensed under this
license.

"You" means the individual or entity exercising rights under this license.

"Licensor" means the copyright holder named above.

2. Grant of Rights

Subject to the restrictions in Section 3, Licensor grants You a worldwide,
royalty-free, non-exclusive license to:

  a. read, study, and audit the Software for any purpose;

  b. copy and run the Software, UNMODIFIED, on computers You own or control,
     to monitor and record matches on Squad game servers You operate or are
     authorized to administer, using an enrollment issued to You by the
     Licensor;

  c. modify a private copy of the Software for the sole purpose of preparing
     a bug report, patch, or pull request intended to be submitted to this
     repository, provided that You do not run the modified copy against the
     Central Service or against a game server whose operator has not agreed.

3. Restrictions

You may NOT, without Licensor's prior written permission:

  a. run a modified copy of the Software (other than as permitted in 2(c)),
     or any other program, in place of the Software against the Central
     Service, or use credentials issued for the Software with any program
     other than the unmodified Software;

  b. send to the Central Service any data that was not read from the game
     server by the unmodified Software -- including fabricated, altered or
     replayed data, or data from a game server You do not operate;

  c. extract, copy, record, decompile, disassemble, reverse engineer, or
     publish the payloads or any other material the Central Service delivers
     to a running agent, or use it for any purpose other than letting that
     agent run -- the fact that such material is delivered to Your machine to
     be executed does not license You to keep, study or share it;

  d. offer the Software, in whole or in part, to any third party as a hosted,
     managed, or "as-a-service" product, or operate a service built on the
     Software for others;

  e. redistribute copies or forks of the Software to third parties, whether
     for a fee or free of charge, other than through this repository's own
     official channel;

  f. remove or alter this license, the copyright notice, or any notice in the
     Software crediting its origin;

  g. use the Software, or anything derived from it or from the Central
     Service, to build a product or service that is materially similar to and
     competes with SquadReplay.

Running the unmodified Software on Your own Squad server(s) to monitor Your
own community's matches -- including a community that charges its own players
or members for access -- is explicitly permitted. Restriction 3(d) targets
reselling or re-hosting SquadReplay's functionality to others, not operating
a Squad game server.

4. Variants and Data Protection

Which variant You run determines what the Software can do (read, write
to the game process's join queue, capture voice). Running a variant is Your
decision and Your responsibility. The voice variants record players' speech;
read LEGAL.md before installing any variant. Nothing in this license replaces
the obligations described there.

